          679.0
        ],
        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "In-plane measurements in the L direction $( \\sigma _ { L } )$were carried out by the four-probe method, whereas the two-probe method was used to measure electrical conductivity in the T direction $( \\sigma _ { T } ,$through plane). The voltage range used for these analyses was kept as close to 0.5–1 VDC as possible, to minimize the occurrence of joule heating. Through-plane measurement of electrical conductivity was done between two gold-plated copper electrodes. Constant DC current was applied while the sample was kept under a constant compressive pressure of 10 MPa and the potential drop was measured between the two electrodes."
      },
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.8
      }
